==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Drone Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Time Traveller Cat''' when obtained from [[A Cat Screaming Love (Merciless)|A Cat Screaming Love]] (guaranteed to drop) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Catway shares range, attack frequency and recharge time with [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Figure Skating Cats]], making this unit very similar, but with drastically worse stats, which makes him replaceable, especially against traits he doesn't target. He is decent against his target traits, especially if you just don't have anything better to replace him with, which can remain true for Angel Enemies for a decent time.

When you acquire this unit early on, it's highly advised to use him against some Angel enemies you struggle, namely [[Winged Pigge]]. But once you get [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Phantom Cat]]'s True Form, Bubble Cat, you don't need him anymore.

One of this unit's only redeeming qualities is his sheer number of [[Cat Combo]]s, making him worth bringing for any, or many, of them alone.

==='''True Form'''===
Time Traveller Cat gains increased damage and health. With this, Time Traveller Cat can finally differentiate itself from Slapstick Cats by dealing significantly higher damage against the traits he targets. Unfortunately, against Red enemies, he gets outclassed by [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]. Against Dark enemies, he gets outclassed by [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]. And against Angel enemies, he gets outclassed by [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] and [[Phantom Cat (Rare Cat)|Bubble Cat]], so he remains obsolete as a midrange specialist. Still, he can provide you as a supplemental DPS dealer in mixed stages, as his effective stats are not too bad for a stackable attacker.

